 ```
 
+### Strict Parsing
+
+Pass `{ strict: true }` to throw an error when a non-empty string cannot be parsed:
+
+```js
+ms('1m', { strict: true })      // 60000
+ms('invalid', { strict: true }) // throws Error: Cannot parse time value. val="invalid"
+ms('invalid')                  // undefined
+```
+
+Only the boolean `true` enables strict parsing. Invalid syntax, unsupported units,
+whitespace-only strings, and strings longer than 100 characters throw in strict
+mode. Numeric formatting is unaffected, and empty strings and invalid input
+types continue to throw regardless of strict mode.
+
 ## Features
 
 - Works both in [Node.js](https://nodejs.org) and in the browser
